</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Chiefron<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 12:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Decided to use my free space for a useful purpose.  <BR> <BR>I used some USGS aerial photos to peice together a mosaic that covers the known crime scenes and drop locations and a comparison map of same scale with yahoo and mapquest maps of the area. <BR> <BR>The big map is pretty large and you ahve to scroll your screen around to see all of it, but I have also made individual scene maps that are zoomed in to 100% of the original USGS photos. <BR> <BR>If you notice any glaring errors in pin placements drop me an e-mail and I will correct them. <BR> <BR><a href="http://home.san.rr.com/illuminatis/" target=_top>http://home.san.rr.com/illuminatis/</a> <BR> <BR>Ron<!--/Text--></td></tr>
